        "config": {
          "text": "SHORT-FORM BRIEF \u2014 edit before running.\nFormat: transformation reveal\nTopic: photography basics\nHook (first 1.5s): [one line]\nPayoff: [one line]\nOn-screen text: [exact copy or leave blank]\nRuntime: 8s, 9:16, sound-on by default."
        },
        "name": "Short-form brief"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_CB6V1JJYK8YY7SVZBDJRAH1T8K",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 1 \u2014 format-native hook planning. The first 1.5 seconds carry the whole retention load."
        },
        "name": "Stage 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_77KXA48A2WD54XY9F39XVRE8SR",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 2100,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 2 \u2014 render, finish and collect. Built for 9:16 sound-on playback."
        },
        "name": "Stage 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_H1ZQ8PNA4FR6AZN081AZCS86AN",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 700,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1400,
          "temperature": 0.82,
          "system_prompt": "You are a short-form creative director writing a transformation reveal about photography basics for a vertical feed.\n\nRETENTION. The first 1.5 seconds must contain a visual question the viewer needs resolved. Plan an explicit beat every 2 to 3 seconds; nothing static may hold longer than that.\n\nFORMAT LAW. Honour the grammar of the transformation reveal \u2014 its native framing, its edit rhythm, and the specific thing audiences expect from it. If the format loops, the last frame must match the first.\n\nCAMERA. Compose 9:16 with the action in the safe centre band. Use a locked-off static frame where only the subject moves on a 24mm wide, framing with a stacked layered composition with three depth planes.\n\nLOOK AND SOUND. Light with blue-hour ambient with a single warm practical for separation; grade as Eterna-style muted greens with gentle highlight roll-off. Specify the sound design in one clause \u2014 what the viewer hears in the first second decides whether they stay.\n\nOUTPUT. Your entire reply is the prompt itself: one dense paragraph, no title, no quotation marks, no trailing notes."
        },
        "name": "Format director"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_CBCMCN0QFJK8J5S2QP9X46Z0Q8",
